WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.150
It’s the year 1325 and the Bologneze and
Modenze armies are about to square off at

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.960
what has been called one of the “bloodiest
medieval battles” in Italy but also one

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.809
of the dumbest, because this was, the war
of the Bucket.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:21.119
To understand why the war started we have
to look at the political climate it started

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:22.119
in.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:25.740
And for that we’ll have to go back all the
way to 800 CE, with the crowning of the first

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.050
Holy Roman Emperor Charlemagne by the bishop
of Rome.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.400
And even though Charlamagne didn’t realise
it back then, his crowning by the bishop of

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.690
Rome set in to motion the centuries long struggle
between the European kingdoms and the church.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.360
Specially as it pertains to the Holy Roman
Empire.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.530
How did this happen?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.490
Well the first thing you have to understand
is that the bishop of Rome is the pope and

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:51.220
Charlemagne was the one who appointed the
bishop of Rome, who was then the one who crowned

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.790
Charlemagne as the Holy Roman Emperor.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:58.760
Which created a weird circular division of
who actually had power over whom.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.690
On top of that Charlemagne's appointment of
the pope, set the precedent of European kings

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:06.939
appointing their own bishops and other church
officials in their own lands, because if a

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:11.070
King can appoint the bishop of Rome why can’t
he then appoint any other bishop.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.469
However Charlemagne also set the precedent
of the pope crowning the Holy Roman Emperor.

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:19.319
So if you were the ruler who controlled the
appointment of the Bishop of Rome, you were

00:01:19.319 --> 00:01:23.810
also the one who controlled the crowning of
the Holy Roman Emperor, in theory anyways.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.229
This resulted in the fact that after Charlemagne
the Germanic and northern italian lands that

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:33.429
became the continuation of the HRE turned
in to a political battleground over the control

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:34.899
of the Papal succession.

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:38.710
With often times the ones who controlled it
being unsurprisingly also the Kings of the

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.100
Germans and Holy Roman Emperors.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.259
But all this, changed around 1050 when the
Papacy actively started to reform the appointment

00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:50.159
of the bishop of Rome and diminish the nobilities
control over them.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:54.281
And when Henry the 4th became the 6 year old
king of the Germans, he clearly didn’t have

00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:58.289
enough experience at the time to handle the
delicate relationship between the king and

00:01:58.289 --> 00:01:59.289
the pope.

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:03.149
So the church council in Rome seized on the
opportunity and restructured the rules of

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:07.930
the Papal succession creating the college
of cardinals as the sole body fit to appoint

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:08.930
a pope.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:13.030
This meant that no longer could a ruler control
the appointment of the pope at least to such

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.270
an extend as they did up until now.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.110
This created many problems within Europe although
I am going to be focusing on just the Holy

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.240
Roman Empire.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.170
For one, Henry the 4th now no longer a kid,
denounced the current pope Gregory the 7th

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.210
as iligitement since he wasn’t appointed
by any king.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:31.940
The Pope on the other hand denounced Henry
the 4th for being an illegitimate ruler of

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.320
the HRE since he wasn’t officially crowned
by the Pope.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.360
On top of that even though the bishop of rome
wasn’t appointed by the nobility anymore,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.950
all the other bishops and church officials
around Europe still where.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.420
Which meant that they were more loyal to their
feudal lord then the church.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.490
The Pope tried to remedy this through several
dubious power grabbing moves of using the

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:54.260
tradition of investitures to control the appointment
of church officials.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.380
This resulted in a lot of political intrigue
and instability throughout europe and even

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.861
a 50 year old civil war in Germany, as the
factions loyal to the nobility and the pope

00:03:02.861 --> 00:03:06.220
fought over who had the rights of appointing
church officials.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.970
It ended in 1122 with an agreement called
the Concordat of Worms.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.900
Where the Nobility could retain some of its
control over the appointment of church officials

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.910
but the Pope was finally recognized as having
some power in the actual appointment process.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:22.950
And even though this treaty settled certain
problems, it resulted in the fact that now

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.080
you had two opposing factions roughly on equal
footing.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.170
Meaning that throughout most of the middle
ages there was lots of continuous political

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.950
maneuvering, intrigue and battles, between
the supporters of the church and the state.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:39.690
And as it pertains to the Italian part of
the HRE, these divisions played a vital part

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.060
in the political landscape of the various
Italian city states.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:48.190
This is because the area was kind of a proxy
battle ground between the HRE and the Papacy.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:53.800
It properly started off 45 years after the
concordat of worms in 1167 with the foundation

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.260
of the Lombard League.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:59.700
This league was a coalition of various Italian
city states that didn’t like the fact that

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.390
the Holy Roman Emperor declared direct imperial
control over them.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.610
And suprise suprise the league was supported
by the Papacy.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:11.420
The Holy Roman Emperor Frederick 1st lead
an army to italy but was defeated by the lombard

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:15.820
league at the battle of Legnano, and had to
sue for peace several years later.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.060
This peace treaty recognized the Holy Roman
Emperor as the ruler of northern Italian city

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:25.570
states, but it also gave the Italian cities
a lot of autonomy, which proved problematic.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.690
This is because after gaining all this autonomy
many, in fact all the Italian city states

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.710
started to have a big rivalry amongst each
other.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.720
And this political environment proved to be
perfect for the next stage of the church vs

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.820
the HRE power struggle.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.230
With cities either starting to be loyal to
the “Church Party” called the Guelphs

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:45.250
(Guelfi) or the imperial party called the
Ghibellines (Ghibellini).

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.160
However these divisions developed their own
little weird dynamics outside of the overarching

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.520
church vs HRE plot.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.210
Cities would sometimes not even care what
each party stood for and chose their allegiances

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:01.240
according to what was the most politically
and economically beneficial to them.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.430
For example the church party tended to be
more prominent in large mercantile cities

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.060
as the Emperor was the main threat to their
wealth and trade networks.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.310
On the other hand the imperial party tended
to be more prominent in smaller cities and

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:17.560
the countryside that often times felt threatened
by the bigger mercantile cities.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:22.690
On top of that, even though some cities where
starch pro church party or pro imperial party,

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.320
other cities didn’t mined switching their
allegiances if it suited them.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.550
Plus some cities had bickering imperial and
church factions that would often times fight

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.070
against each other over the control of the
city.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:36.750
And even though it was the power struggle
between the Holy Roman Emperor and Pope that

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.930
started these parties, the northern italian
city states took it up a notch.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.450
Your allegiance to one or the other party
started to affect many other things outside

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.340
of just your pro church or pro empire leanings.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:53.190
Any big and small issues or disagreements
started to be split amongst party lines.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.340
And not just that, depending on what party
you were associated with, it affected what

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:02.060
taverns and shops you where allowed in to,
what cities you could trade in, how you dressed

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:07.270
and what side you put the feather on your
hat on, and even the way you cut certain fruits.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:12.470
The allegiances of some cities to its party
bacem so strong that you can tell what party

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.740
a city supported by just looking at its coat
of arms today.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.340
If has a white cross on a red field it supported
the imperial party, if it had a red cross

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.960
on a white field it supported the church party.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.860
These divisions came to a boiling point during
the 13th century interregnum of the Holy Roman

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.860
Empire.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:34.060
This was a 67 years long succession crisis
within the HRE where the princes were unable

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.720
to agree on a new king.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:40.150
This instability combined with the various
pretender kings and the continues power struggle

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.620
between the HRE and the papacy was the final
straw for northern italy.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.520
And even though there were battles between
the imperial and church factions prior to

00:06:48.520 --> 00:07:08.590
the interregnum, the interregnum period took
it in to an overdrive.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:18.199
The imperial vs church faction struggle took
a bit of a respite after the 1289 church party

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:20.180
win at the Battle of Campaldino.

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:24.240
This battle drastically diminished the power
and consequently the threat of the imperial

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.919
party in Italy, and because Florence was the
one leading the church faction in this battle,

00:07:28.919 --> 00:07:32.570
they became a prominent if not the main power
within the party.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:37.199
But now since the church party seemingly won,
with the imperial party being on its back

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:38.199
foot.

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:42.640
The Florentine church faction ironically started
to be concerned with the increasing Papal

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.270
influence within the city.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.460
So a split within the church faction happened.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:50.550
With the supporters for more papal control
being called black guelphs (black church party)

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:54.010
and the supporters for less papal control
being called white guelphs (white church party).

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:57.860
The black church party with the support of
the pope eventually won and most of the white

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.199
church party members were exiled from the
city.

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:05.120
Which included the famous Dante who after
his exile went on to write the Dante’s inferno.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.229
But I digress.

00:08:06.229 --> 00:08:10.660
Even though this church party division was
most prominent in Florence it showed the underlying

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.419
problems and disunity within the faction.

00:08:13.419 --> 00:08:17.669
And the imperial party wasn’t any better
with Emperor Henry 7th stating that he was

00:08:17.669 --> 00:08:23.130
disgusted by both sides actions, pointing
out how some members strayed vary far from

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.850
the initial party goals.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:29.229
This was because at this point the church
and imperial parties meant much more and many

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:33.099
other things to many other people then just
the power struggle between the church and

00:08:33.099 --> 00:08:34.450
the Holy Roman Empire.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:38.950
Plus if you think about it, it isn’t that
big of a stretch that after so much fighting

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:43.990
through multiple generations, the reasons
for ones loyalty to their party became skewed

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.510
to say the least.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:50.560
So at the start of the 14th century, the prelude
to the war of the bucket, was a multiple centuries

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:55.310
long power struggle between the church and
the Holy Roman Empire that turned so out of

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:00.610
hand and created so many feuds in northern
Italy, that now even the Pope and the Emperor

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.710
denounced some of the acts committed by both
factions.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:05.570
Hope you enjoyed the video.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:11.240
To be honest the whole church vs empire factions
of medieval Italy is a subject so complex

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.960
many of dissertations have been written on
it and therefor I had to skip or simplifi

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:20.620
a lot of nuencoses or details that shaped
certain overarching decisions.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.120
Thus there’s a lot of footnotes in the description
that are trying to explain some of it and

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.090
if you want to know more there’re always
sources in my scripts.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:30.520
Lastly, if you’re looking forward to the
War of the Bucket video that will be coming

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:35.680
out on my channel at some point, consider
subscribing and maybe hitting that bell icon,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:41.860
because the truth is, the war of bucket, actually
did not happen as portrayed in all of these

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:42.880
youtube videos.

